_vs_hist":0.02885299802211623,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":63.9,"_gate_piotroski":6,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":66.7,"_gate_spread":-0.028969392177815537,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.504292546619877,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":16.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.07809187623028065,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":42.7,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.06092177204579771,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":53.6,"_gate_pool_share":0.49579638494088396,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.07106452672944785,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":60.5,"_gate_margins":0.014532376566545218,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":64.5,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0329402752838975,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":47.7,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.013500737295697007,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":66.9,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.00692728959991635,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":88.5,"_gate_insider_own":0.00217,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":1.4,"_gate_insider_buying":0.25,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":25.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Ingersoll Rand Inc. provides mission-critical air, fluid, clean energy, and medical technologies services and solutions worldwide. It operates in two segments, Industrial Technologies and Services, and Precision and Science Technologies. The Industrial Technologies and Services segment designs, manufactures, markets, and services a range of air and gas compression and treatment equipment, vacuum and blower products, fluid transfer equipment, loading systems, and power tools and lifting equipment; and other specialized equipment, including aftermarket parts, consumables and services, air treatment equipment, controls, other accessories, and services under the Ingersoll Rand, Gardner Denver, Nash, CompAir, Elmo Rietschle, and other brands. The Precision and Science Technologies segment designs, manufactures, and markets diaphragm, piston, water-powered, peristaltic, gear, vane, progressive cavity, and syringe pumps; and gas boosters, hydrogen compression systems, liquid handling systems, odorant injection systems, controls, software, and other related components and accessories for precision dosing, liquid and solid transfer, dispensing, gas compression and sampling, pressure management, flow control, powder handling, and other applications under the Air Dimensions, Albin, ARO, Dosatron, Haskel, Ingersoll Rand, LMI, Maximus, Milton Roy, MP, Oberdorfer, Seepex, Thomas, Welch, Williams, YZ, and Zinnser Analytic brands. This segment's products are used in medical, laboratory, industrial manufacturing, water and wastewater, chemical processing, clean energy, food and beverage, agriculture and other markets. It sells its products through a network of direct sales representatives and independent distributors. It has a strategic alliance with Garrett Motion. The company was formerly known as Gardner Denver Holdings, Inc. and changed its name to Ingersoll Rand Inc. in March 2020. Ingersoll Rand Inc. was founded in 1859 and is headquartered in Davidson, North Carolina.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Vicente  Reynal | Chairman, CEO & President | Age 50 | Compensation: $2.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 21K people. Revenue per employee of $364K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers, improving at 16%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $58K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Ingersoll Rand Inc. is a large-cap industrials business with a $31.9B market cap on $7.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +9% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 39%.","The business throws off $1.2B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 16 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.33\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 4.5\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 3.3% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries a 32% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.3154311649016641},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $13.6M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-13623796.08},{"text":"Significant goodwill (46% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Ingersoll Rand (IR) Could Be 13% Undervalued As Earnings And Guidance Impress","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-ir/ingersoll-rand/news/ingersoll-rand-ir-could-be-13-undervalued-as-earnings-and-gu","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793964584.958,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.926,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Ingersoll Rand (IR) \u2013 Analysts\u2019 Weekly Ratings Updates","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/ingersoll-rand-ir-analysts-weekly-ratings-updates.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793818618.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.052,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Ingersoll Rand Inc. $IR Stock Sold by Sumitomo Mitsui Trust Group Inc.","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/ingersoll-rand-inc-ir-stock-sold-by-sumitomo-mitsui-trust-group-inc.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793788402.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.955,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Does Earnings Beat Change The Bull Case For Ingersoll Rand Stock (IR)?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-ir/ingersoll-rand/news/does-earnings-beat-change-the-bull-case-for-ingersoll-rand-s-1","date":"2026-11-01","timestamp":1793525582.072,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.869,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":