.2B of cash against $4.8B of debt), above the 1.5x gate, with interest covered 4.5x.","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 3.3, in the safe zone).","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 2.06).","Goodwill makes up 46% of assets, a soft asset exposed to impairment."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 8.9% over 3 years and 9.3% over 5 years, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 32%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 7.1% a year over five years.","Margins are expanding (+1.3% trend).","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 9%.","Capex runs only 0.3x depreciation (1.8% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.2%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insider trading is two-way: 1 purchase and 3 sales over the past year, net $13.6M sold.","It returns 3.3% a year to shareholders (3.2% in buybacks and 0.1% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 1.4% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 21,000 employees, each generates about $364K of revenue, in line with the Industrials median, and productivity has risen 15.7% a year.","That works out to $58K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $2.7M (7x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (3/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $3K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":50,"head":"Watch: trades 17% above fair value of $71.13.","pros":["FCF margin 15.9%","Revenue grew 9.3%/yr over 5y","Altman Z in the safe zone","Operating margin expanding 1.3%/yr","Returns 3.3% a year to shareholders"],"cons":["Trades 17% above fair value of $71.13","ROIC 6.5% vs WACC 9.4%","EV/EBITDA 17.4x vs sector 13.3x"],"flags":[],"need":["the model rates it HOLD","no margin of safety","i